exploratory enquiry of feasible size and cost. In one such study, where very little was
recorded about the agriculture, the maps available were divided into segments of 6
kilometres side and one tenth of these were chosen at random. These were sent to their
localities and the local agricultural experts were asked to give details of the type of cropping
