employees'part.
In the course of this instruction it would be worthwhile to watch for two kinds ofspecial
skills emerging. One, the man who is by temperament suitable for a role of greater
responsibility in local supervision, and the other, one who is capable of special skill but not
necessarily in the supervisory direction. For instance, a man may be particularly skilful in
surveying with compass and chain and it might be worth noting him as a possible specialist in
