and the man who stuck out and got increased attention. Explicit care should be taken to
maintain the position of the enumerator who has got to live with the situation after his
senior has departed.
It is too much to hope that the senior staff in the control organisation will be able to find
time to travel extensively, but before closing this section the very great benefit of personal
contact should be underlined. It has been found in numerous instances in developing
countries and it applies equally effectively in developed countries. Visits from a statistician
to a neighbourhood more than once notably increased the proportion of a sample
questionnaire which was returned. Visits to voluntary crop reporters has increased the care
with which they complete their routine questionnaires.If a chance presents itself for contact
of this kind it should certainly be taken and ifit does not present itself at least every twelve months,or so, an occasion should be explicitly created.




