supervisors and, through them, headquarters with early warning of the need to prepare new
supplies. Such preparations may require a new plate or stencil to be made if the old one has
been worked out or if modifications are necessary.
Equipment
This can be classified in a number of groups according to its size,or the place it occupies
in the work done. The group includes computers;desk calculating machines;typewriters and
reproduction equipment; smaller items of equipment for central office use including
planimeters, rulers, protractors, pencils, pegboards, stationery and all associated filing
facilities; basic stationery required by field staff including pencils, rubbers, rulers, etc.;
compasses, chains, measuring wheels, and weighing equipment for crop cutting and the
necessary receptacles for carrying it; transport whether land rovers, motorcycles, or
bicycles. A check list of a number of these items is given in Appendix G.Each might be the
