and measuring the plots. Generally speaking, a two or three man team could measure 12
plots a day, but this could be increased to 15 under pressure or under favourable conditions.
Statistics of development schemes
The above discussion is written with largely unorganised development conditions in mind.
However, there are many examples to be found of rather closely controlled developments.
It is extremely important when any such schemes are planned that specific provision should
be made for the collection of the statistics necessary to describe their progress,physical and
financial. Evaluation should then be possible both from the overall standpoint and that of
the farms and families which are concerned.




